Card Glint integration for Manabrew

Source: https://github.com/vishvananda/card-glint
Revision: b541b67e7d694a58ae222f14d91bec4110f71af7 (0.3.10)
Code license: MIT OR Apache-2.0. The original license texts, upstream notice
and Magic asset notice accompany this package without relicensing.

Run yarn ensure:card-glint to build the local dependency. yarn install runs it
automatically, as do frontend development, type-check and build entry points.
Prerequisites: Node 24+, npm, Git, tar, Rustup and a native C/C++ build toolchain.
The script installs Rust 1.98.0 with wasm32-unknown-unknown and a private
wasm-bindgen-cli 0.2.127. npm ci uses the pinned source's package-lock.json;
Cargo uses its Cargo.lock with --locked. The downloaded archive must match
the SHA-256 in upstream.json. No floating branch or runtime module URL is used.

Source and tool caches live in node_modules/.cache/card-glint. Generated runtime,
matching WASM and declarations live in dist/ under this local package. The root
link: dependency refers to that directory rather than a stale copied package.
The completion key hashes the source pin, package manifest, both build scripts
and every patch. dist/provenance.json records the input hashes. Generated output
is not committed. A missing artifact triggers the build again.

Local modifications:
- patches/rules-text.patch adds the public CardTextureInput.rulesText option.
  Its default preserves upstream painting. false suppresses rules, flavor and
  embedded rules symbols without changing face input, frame choice or layout.
  Manabrew uses this backing under its interactive rules layer.
  Native Leveler level labels remain painted when rules ink is omitted.
  Class level header bands are also suppressed in the text-free pass, while
  the native rules paper remains. The host reuses the native band asset and
  measured typography in scrolling level rows; printed rendering is unchanged.
- patches/host-geometry.patch exposes the painter's existing Adventure rules,
  Prepared spell and Flip panel rectangles through the public presentation
  entry. It preserves paint geometry and lets host interactions use the same
  bounds instead of approximating them.
  It also honors explicit reverse-face statistics for Saga layout selection,
  preserving transforming Saga statistics when localized type text requires
  an explicit semantic layout.
  Shared Saga marker metrics and reminder/chapter columns are exported from
  the same constants used by the native painter and layout. Host chapter
  badges therefore occupy the printed gutter without changing rules bounds.
- patches/finish-material.patch exposes modern surface materials, shared
  resources and deterministic wear. Artwork-derived masks and caustics support
  all nine finishes; generated artwork and printing remain separate so optical
  distortion does not blur rules text. Wear composites above finished printing.
- patches/special-layout.patch paints Room, Planar, Scheme and Vanguard with
  semantic bounds with explicit face ownership and separate Room door rules.
  Art Series and Front Card remain scan-backed.
- patches/integration-exports.patch exposes the semantic layout helpers and
  source corner geometry used by the host's flat and full 3D renderers.
- patches/zz-live-changes.patch adds optional host-resolved live-state ink.
  Native power/toughness values and added type words are tinted independently;
  removed-only type changes tint the remaining type line. Text shaping, frame
  bounds and unannotated painting stay unchanged. Recursive face cache keys
  and optical printing retain the annotations.
  Manabrew supplies its invariant gameTheme.cardChange palette without glow
  or brightness adjustment. The optional omitInk pass retains native paper
  and unselected text while omitting only live-highlighted glyphs.
  The host caches cropped native paper and transparent word/stat ink layers.
  Pixi uses GSAP to scale and float only that ink; DOM uses matching transform
  animation. Paper, frames and art remain stationary. Animation never
  recomposes the card, and disabled motion retains the complete static face.
- patches/offline-assets.patch provides one host asset resolver for Canvas2D,
  historical SVG preparation and the full 3D renderer's AssetStore. Its public
  magic/offline-assets entry enumerates actual per-face resources and all 13
  CSS/programmatic font faces. The host registers fonts from fetched bytes,
  not remote CSS, and stores explicit user downloads in browser Cache Storage.
  Per-deck manifests include both faces, selected art/scans, current cosmetics,
  localized card records, common-rarity stamp vectors, the hologram mask
  source, interactive mana symbols and the standard card back. React original
  images and Pixi image/mana loaders consult the same persistent asset cache.
  Finish waves, wear and etched edge maps are generated locally.
- bundle-card-glint.mjs builds the browser, Magic, presentation, finish,
  offline-assets and kernels entries, plus upstream TypeScript declarations.
  It omits the showcase website. Generated WASM glue imports matching modules
  through Vite ?url assets, so production JS and WASM receive content hashes
  together instead of resolving an untracked relative WASM filename.
- The macOS linker wrapper follows Ironsmith's integration at revision
  d3185228d944ee16c030c292ff35376f7a3fe334, setting the pinned toolchain's
  LLVM library path only for its WASM linker invocation.

Magic frames, fonts and symbols remain external references pinned by upstream.
They are not copied into this package and are not covered by its code license.
Some references point to MSE asset collections; no MSE interpreter, scripts,
corpus or runtime package is shipped. See MAGIC-NOTICE for rights and sources.
Original card scans and art retain their owners' rights.

