No external asset binaries are redistributed by the installer. Downloads go
directly from the original pinned sources to the user's device only after an
explicit permission acknowledgement. Availability on GitHub does not establish
permission; users must have the required rights. There is no claim that a
first-ever disconnected launch can obtain missing assets.

Settings > Cache > Generated cards offline installs one saved deck and language.
A complete manifest is written only after every requested image/font decodes
and is stored. Cancellation/failure preserves partial files for a later retry
but never publishes a complete manifest. Cold starts read cached fonts, frames,
art and exact localized records; readiness checks the manifest's actual cache
entries. Deck/printing/cosmetic/language changes require another installation.
Clear renderer cache removes these assets, records and manifests, not desktop
cardArtCache downloads. Already open renderers can retain in-memory resources
until reload. This cache does not install the application shell or engine.

Vite emits these notices, licenses and build provenance into card-glint-licenses/
in the frontend distribution. To update the source, review the upstream source
and notices, update upstream.json and the package version, review all patches,
then run yarn ensure:card-glint and the application's build and browser checks.
